   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter">
                <div type="mainBody">
                    <opener>
                        <dateline>c/o <name type="person" key="leon93">Paul Léon</name>  <lb/>Paris the <date when="1934-04-24">24-th of April 1934</date> <lb/>John Gadsby C.B.E. Esq. <lb/>Tokyo. </dateline>
                        <lb/>
                        <salute>Dear Sir, </salute> </opener>
                    <p>I beg to acknowledge receipt through Mr Paul Léon of cheque for the equivalent of 400 Yen representing the proceeds from my claim against the <choice>
                            <sic>japanese</sic>
                            <corr>Japanese</corr>
                        </choice> pirates of <name type="work" key="W_ULYSSES">ULYSSES</name> and to thank you for your intervention in this affair. </p> <closer>
                        <salute>Believe me<lb/>sincerely yours</salute>
                    </closer>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div type="notes">
                <note xml:id="global-note1" type="global">This letter has been transcribed from a typed carbon copy. It was sent as an enclosure with the <rs type="letter" key="L_70390">letter from Paul Léon of 24 April 1934</rs>.</note>
            </div>
      </body>
